  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), panel mounted on the VIPER TQS, seen from its lower end and the left: toggle rows nearest the camera, jettison button and gear lever section at the upper right",
  "mappingSource": "VIPER PANEL user manual (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/Viper/VIPER_PANEL_User_Manual.pdf) p.8 \"Mapping of the 32 buttons and 1 axis in mode A\": 1 jettison button, 17 gear lever; row 1: toggle 2/3, rotary 9-12, rotary 4-8; row 2: squares 13 14 / 15 16, wheel B1 (axis); row 3: 24, 25/26; row 4: 27, 28, rotary 18-20; row 5: 29/30, 31/32, encoder 21 cw / 22 ccw / 23 push",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The photo is taken along the panel's length, so the rows run left to right and the columns run toward the upper right; the toggle rows were matched by their base rings. Mode B (virtual buttons, manual p.9) changes the numbering; the catalog follows mode A. Of the 2x2 square pushbuttons only the upper pair (13, 14) is clearly visible; 15 is partly hidden by the toggles, 16 hidden. The rotary positions share one spot per knob.",
